            "review_title": "Review at Chu Quan Bbq Grill",
            "review_text": "Alex H\nHertfordshire, United Kingdom2573 contributions\n4\nTwo experiences, not bad\nMar 2020 • Couples\nWe came here the first time when we got off the bus in Da Lat after a 6 hour journey and we were hungry.\nThey bring out a strange looking bread with a spicey dip, which is actually added to the bill at the end for very cheap, but without telling you.\nWe ordered a beef stir fry vegetables and noodles, which was quite reasonably priced, and two Saigon beers (18,000 per small can).\nThis food was very tasty and it made us come back the next day.\nFrom the staff being very nice and welcoming on the first day, the second day seemed to change, although I’m not sure if it was something to do with the corona virus outbreak as we had experienced some hostility towards tourists at this time.\nThe next days food was nowhere near as good and the service was so poor, we really didn’t feel welcome at all. We had two budweiser cans for 25,000 and they were so warm and watery.\nAll in all perhaps try this place for yourself but don’t go out of your way to visit.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 15, 2020",
